{"text":"And yet, we wonder why boys are more likely to steal money from their parents. What if both boys and girls were raised not to link masculinity with money? What if the attitude was not, the boy has to pay, but rather, whoever has more should pay? Now, of course, because of the historical advantage, it is mostly men who will have more today, but if we start raising children differently, then in 50 years, in 100 years, boys will no longer have the pressure of having to prove this masculinity. But by far, the worst thing we do to males by making them feel that they have to be hard is that we leave them with very fragile egos. The more hard man a man feels compelled to be, the weaker his ego is.","words":[{"text":"And","start":0.0,"end":0.64},{"text":"yet","start":0.64,"end":0.78,"punct":","},{"text":"we","start":0.82,"end":0.94},{"text":"wonder","start":0.94,"end":1.18},{"text":"why","start":1.18,"end":1.48},{"text":"boys","start":1.48,"end":1.9},{"text":"are","start":1.9,"end":2.06},{"text":"more","start":2.06,"end":2.2},{"text":"likely","start":2.2,"end":2.44},{"text":"to","start":2.44,"end":2.66},{"text":"steal","start":2.66,"end":3.0},{"text":"money","start":3.0,"end":3.24},{"text":"from","start":3.24,"end":3.46},{"text":"their","start":3.46,"end":3.64},{"text":"parents","start":3.64,"end":4.0,"punct":"."},{"text":"What","start":6.28,"end":6.48},{"text":"if","start":6.48,"end":6.74},{"text":"both","start":6.74,"end":7.16},{"text":"boys","start":7.16,"end":7.94},{"text":"and","start":7.94,"end":8.24},{"text":"girls","start":8.24,"end":8.68},{"text":"were","start":8.68,"end":9.04},{"text":"raised","start":9.04,"end":9.5},{"text":"not","start":9.5,"end":10.18},{"text":"to","start":10.18,"end":10.48},{"text":"link","start":10.48,"end":10.64},{"text":"masculinity","start":10.64,"end":11.1},{"text":"with","start":11.1,"end":11.54},{"text":"money","start":11.54,"end":11.82,"punct":"?"},{"text":"What","start":12.62,"end":12.96},{"text":"if","start":12.96,"end":13.1